# 6️⃣ How to explain this to business (script you can use)

Here’s a clean, non-technical explanation:

> “There are changes that affect *what the system means*, and changes that affect *where the data goes*. We’re giving you control over the second category in real time, but the first category needs rigor because mistakes there silently corrupt data.”

If you want to sound even stronger:

> “Anything that changes interpretation goes through review. Anything that changes routing can be done safely in the UI.”

This usually lands very well.

---

# 7️⃣ Why letting business edit intents directly is dangerous (rationale)

Use these points if you need to push back:

* LLM behavior changes are non-linear
* Small prompt edits can cause large extraction drift
* Errors propagate silently downstream
* Audit & explainability are lost
* Rollback is ambiguous (“what changed?”)

This is not theoretical — this is where AI platforms get burned.

